          ":question/id": "f9f879b2-0f95-56b8-b2ba-e085bebf3f59",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $5w-8=-w+8$\n- **II.** $7w+3=7w$\n- **III.** $7w+2=7w+2$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5w-8 & =-w+8 \\\\ 5w-8+w+8 & =-w+8+w+8 \\\\ 6w & =16 \\\\ w & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $5w-8=-w+8$ has the unique solution $w=\\frac{8}{3}.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7w+3 & =7w \\\\ 7w+3-7w & =7w-7w \\\\ 3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $w.$ Therefore, the equation $7w+3=7w$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7w+2 & =7w+2 \\\\ 7w+2-7w & =7w+2-7w \\\\ 2 & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $w.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
