          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-7z-1=-7z-6$\n- **II.** $7z+5=7z+5$\n- **III.** $7z+3=-3z-6$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7z-1 & =-7z-6 \\\\ -7z-1+7z & =-7z-6+7z \\\\ -1 & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $z.$ Therefore, the equation $-7z-1=-7z-6$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7z+5 & =7z+5 \\\\ 7z+5-7z & =7z+5-7z \\\\ 5 & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $z.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7z+3 & =-3z-6 \\\\ 7z+3+3z-3 & =-3z-6+3z-3 \\\\ 10z & =-9 \\\\ z & =- \\frac{9}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $7z+3=-3z-6$ has the unique solution $z=- \\frac{9}{10}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
